<section>
    <h3>What the review changed</h3>
    <table class="compare" style="font-size: 0.55em;">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th style="width: 18%"></th>
                <th>First version</th>
                <th>Today</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td>Secrets</td>
                <td class="bad"><code>Authorization</code>, cookies, tokens written as is</td>
                <td class="good">Redacted by default, request and response</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td>Missing entry</td>
                <td class="bad">Real network call by default, silently</td>
                <td class="good">Exception, never the network</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td><code>stream()</code></td>
                <td class="bad">Broken, and <code>getContent()</code> serialised the requests</td>
                <td class="good"><code>AsyncResponse</code>, recorded chunk after chunk</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="fragment">
                <td>Options</td>
                <td class="bad"><code>timeout: 5</code> became 60 s when recording</td>
                <td class="good">Original options passed through as is</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <aside class="notes">
        <p>So, what did the review change?</p>
        <p>[click] Secrets. Before: written as they are. Today: redacted by default.</p>
        <p>[click] A missing request. Before: a real call, silently. Today: an exception, never the network.</p>
        <p>[click] stream(). Before: broken, and no more parallel requests. Today: recorded chunk by chunk.</p>
        <p>[click] Options. Before: a timeout of 5 seconds became 60 when recording. Today: options pass as they are.</p>
        <p>The lesson: a decorator must be invisible. And every line here is a bug found by a reviewer who ran the code. Not just read it: ran it.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
